      cards: [
        { q: "Picture 1. Egg from stool. Identify, fertile or infertile?", a: "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", wrong: ["<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", "<b><i>Taenia</i></b> sp.<br>About 45 × 30 µm. Thick, smooth, <b>striated</b> shell; oncosphere with <b>6 hooks</b>.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo."], img: "cards/p1/p1_00.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 2. Egg from stool. Identify, fertile or infertile?", a: "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", wrong: ["<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", "<b><i>Taenia</i></b> sp.<br>About 45 × 30 µm. Thick, smooth, <b>striated</b> shell; oncosphere with <b>6 hooks</b>.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo."], img: "cards/p1/p1_01.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 3. Egg with a thick, bumpy coat. Identify, fertile or infertile?", a: "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", wrong: ["<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", "<b><i>Taenia</i></b> sp.<br>About 45 × 30 µm. Thick, smooth, <b>striated</b> shell; oncosphere with <b>6 hooks</b>.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo."], img: "cards/p1/p1_02.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 4. Identify this egg.", a: "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", wrong: ["<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", "<b><i>Taenia</i></b> sp.<br>About 45 × 30 µm. Thick, smooth, <b>striated</b> shell; oncosphere with <b>6 hooks</b>.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo."], img: "cards/p1/p1_03.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 5. Long, irregular egg from stool. Identify.", a: "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", wrong: ["<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed.", "<b><i>Fasciola hepatica</i> / <i>Fasciolopsis buski</i></b> egg (identical)<br>About 150 × 80 µm. Yellow-brown, ovoid, contents fill out to the shell, indistinct operculum. <i>F. hepatica</i> = sheep liver fluke (sheep & cattle). <i>F. buski</i> = pigs."], img: "cards/p1/p1_04.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 6. Identify this egg.", a: "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", wrong: ["<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed.", "<b><i>Fasciola hepatica</i> / <i>Fasciolopsis buski</i></b> egg (identical)<br>About 150 × 80 µm. Yellow-brown, ovoid, contents fill out to the shell, indistinct operculum. <i>F. hepatica</i> = sheep liver fluke (sheep & cattle). <i>F. buski</i> = pigs."], img: "cards/p1/p1_05.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 7. Barrel-shaped egg with a plug at each end. Identify.", a: "<b><i>Trichuris trichiura</i></b> (whipworm)<br>About 54 × 22 µm. Barrel / football shape with a clear plug at each end.", wrong: ["<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", "<b><i>Clonorchis sinensis</i></b> (Chinese liver fluke)<br>About 30 × 15 µm, the smallest egg. Shouldered operculum, small knob at the other end."], img: "cards/p1/p1_06.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 8. Thin-shelled egg with a dividing embryo. Identify.<br><i>Clue: 60 x 40 µm</i>", a: "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", wrong: ["<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed.", "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside."], img: "cards/p1/p1_07.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 9. Identify this egg.<br><i>Clue: 60 x 40</i>", a: "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", wrong: ["<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed.", "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, fertile egg<br>About 65 × 45 µm. Round to oval with a thick, bumpy (mammillated) coat.", "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside."], img: "cards/p1/p1_08.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 10. Thin-shelled egg next to a 100 µm scale bar. Identify.", a: "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed.", wrong: ["<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside."], img: "cards/p1/p1_13.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 11. Identify this egg.", a: "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed.", wrong: ["<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", "<b><i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i></b>, infertile egg<br>About 90 × 40 µm. Longer and narrower than the fertile egg, irregular coat, disorganized granules inside.", "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside."], img: "cards/p1/p1_14.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 12. Egg flattened on one side. Identify.", a: "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside.", wrong: ["<b><i>Trichuris trichiura</i></b> (whipworm)<br>About 54 × 22 µm. Barrel / football shape with a clear plug at each end.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed."], img: "cards/p1/p1_09.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 13. Identify this egg.", a: "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside.", wrong: ["<b><i>Trichuris trichiura</i></b> (whipworm)<br>About 54 × 22 µm. Barrel / football shape with a clear plug at each end.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed."], img: "cards/p1/p1_10.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 14. Eggs from a tape prep. Identify.", a: "<b><i>Enterobius vermicularis</i></b> (pinworm)<br>About 55 × 25 µm. Flattened on one side, larva often visible inside.", wrong: ["<b><i>Trichuris trichiura</i></b> (whipworm)<br>About 54 × 22 µm. Barrel / football shape with a clear plug at each end.", "<b>Hookworm</b> (<i>Necator americanus</i>) egg<br>About 60 × 40 µm, smaller than <i>Trichostrongylus</i>. Thin clear shell with a gap around the dividing embryo.", "<b><i>Trichostrongylus</i></b> sp. egg<br>About 88 × 45 µm. Larger and more elongated (ovoid) than a hookworm egg, slightly pointed."], img: "cards/p1/p1_11.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 15. Mouthparts: name the worm on the left and on the right.", a: "<b>Hookworm mouthparts</b><br>Left: <i>Ancylostoma duodenale</i> (<b>teeth</b>). Right: <i>Necator americanus</i> (<b>cutting plates</b>).", wrong: ["<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, rhabditiform larva<br>“Short & sexy”: <b>short</b> buccal cavity and esophagus, <b>large genital primordium</b>, pointed tail.", "<b>Hookworm</b>, rhabditiform larva<br><b>Long</b> buccal cavity, bulbed esophagus, small genital primordium.", "<b>Hookworm</b>, filariform larva<br>Long buccal cavity, no bulb, <b>pointed</b> tail."], img: "cards/p1/p1_12.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 16. Larva in stool. Identify the organism and the form.", a: "<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, rhabditiform larva<br>“Short & sexy”: <b>short</b> buccal cavity and esophagus, <b>large genital primordium</b>, pointed tail.", wrong: ["<b>Hookworm</b>, rhabditiform larva<br><b>Long</b> buccal cavity, bulbed esophagus, small genital primordium.", "<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, filariform larva<br><b>Notched tail</b>, long esophagus (about 40% of body length), no bulb.", "<b>Hookworm</b>, filariform larva<br>Long buccal cavity, no bulb, <b>pointed</b> tail."], img: "cards/p1/p1_15.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 17. Larva. Identify the organism and the form.", a: "<b>Hookworm</b>, rhabditiform larva<br><b>Long</b> buccal cavity, bulbed esophagus, small genital primordium.", wrong: ["<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, rhabditiform larva<br>“Short & sexy”: <b>short</b> buccal cavity and esophagus, <b>large genital primordium</b>, pointed tail.", "<b>Hookworm</b>, filariform larva<br>Long buccal cavity, no bulb, <b>pointed</b> tail.", "<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, filariform larva<br><b>Notched tail</b>, long esophagus (about 40% of body length), no bulb."], img: "cards/p1/p1_17.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 18. Larva with a close-up of the tail. Identify the organism and the form.", a: "<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, filariform larva<br><b>Notched tail</b>, long esophagus (about 40% of body length), no bulb.", wrong: ["<b>Hookworm</b>, filariform larva<br>Long buccal cavity, no bulb, <b>pointed</b> tail.", "<b><i>Strongyloides stercoralis</i></b>, rhabditiform larva<br>“Short & sexy”: <b>short</b> buccal cavity and esophagus, <b>large genital primordium</b>, pointed tail.", "<b>Hookworm</b>, rhabditiform larva<br><b>Long</b> buccal cavity, bulbed esophagus, small genital primordium."], img: "cards/p1/p1_16.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 19. Strongyloides vs hookworm: how do you tell the rhabditiform and filariform larvae apart?", a: "<b>Rhabditiform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = short buccal cavity, large genital primordium. Hookworm = long buccal cavity, small genital primordium. Both have a bulb.<br><b>Filariform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = <b>notched</b> tail. Hookworm = <b>pointed</b> tail. Neither has a bulb.", wrong: ["<b>Rhabditiform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = long buccal cavity, small genital primordium. Hookworm = short buccal cavity, large genital primordium.<br><b>Filariform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = pointed tail. Hookworm = notched tail.", "<b>Rhabditiform:</b> both have a long buccal cavity; only hookworm has a bulb.<br><b>Filariform:</b> both have a notched tail; tell them apart by size.", "<b>Rhabditiform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = short buccal cavity, no genital primordium. Hookworm = long buccal cavity, large genital primordium.<br><b>Filariform:</b> both have a bulbed esophagus."], img: "cards/p1/p1_18.jpg" },
        { q: "Picture 20. Fill in the chart: buccal cavity, bulb, tail and genital primordium for the four larvae.", a: "<b>Rhabditiform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = short buccal cavity, large genital primordium. Hookworm = long buccal cavity, small genital primordium. Both have a bulb.<br><b>Filariform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = <b>notched</b> tail. Hookworm = <b>pointed</b> tail. Neither has a bulb.", wrong: ["<b>Rhabditiform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = long buccal cavity, small genital primordium. Hookworm = short buccal cavity, large genital primordium.<br><b>Filariform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = pointed tail. Hookworm = notched tail.", "<b>Rhabditiform:</b> both have a long buccal cavity; only hookworm has a bulb.<br><b>Filariform:</b> both have a notched tail; tell them apart by size.", "<b>Rhabditiform:</b> <i>Strongyloides</i> = short buccal cavity, no genital primordium. Hookworm = long buccal cavity, large genital primordium.<br><b>Filariform:</b> both have a bulbed esophagus."], img: "cards/p1/p1_19.jpg" }
      ]
