        { q: "Disadvantages: not suitable for some permanent Trichrome smears, inadequate preservation of protozoan trophs, can interfere with PCR (esp after extended fixation time)", a: "10% Formalin" },
        { q: "Advantages: components both fix and stain organisms, easy to prepare, long shelf life, used for field surveys, suitable for concentration procedures", a: "MIF (merthiolate-iodine-formaldehyde)" },
        { q: "Disadvantages: not suitable for Trichrome, inadequate preservation of morphology of protozoan trophs, iodine can interfere with other stains and fluorescence and may cause distortion of protozoa", a: "MIF (merthiolate-iodine-formaldehyde)" },
        { q: "Advantages: good preservation of morphology of protozoan trophs & cysts, easy preparation of permanent smears stained with Trichrome (preservative and fixative), preserved samples are stable for several months", a: "LV-PVA (low viscosity polyvinyl alcohol)" },
        { q: "Disadvantages: inadequate preservation of morphology of helminth eggs and larvae and coccidia and microsporidia, contains mercuric chloride, difficult and expensive to prepare and dispose of, not good for concentration, can't use with immunoassay kits, not suitable for acid-fast, safranin, or chromotrope stains", a: "LV-PVA" },
        { q: "Advantages: suitable for both concentration procedures and prep of permanent stained smears, easy to prepare, long shelf life, suitable for acid fast safranin and chromotrope stains, compatible with immunoassay kits", a: "SAF (sodium acetate-acetic acid-formalin)" },
        { q: "Disadvantages: requires additive (like albumin-glycerin) for adhesion of specimen to slides, permanent stains not as good as with others", a: "SAF (sodium acetate-acetic acid-formalin)" },
        { q: "Advantages: good preservation of morphology of protozoan trophs and cysts, easy prep of permanent stained smears", a: "Schaudinn's Fixative" },
        { q: "Disadvantages: less suitable for concentration procedures, contains mercuric chloride, inadequate preservation of morphology of helminth eggs and larvae, coccidia, and microsporidia, poor adhesion of liquid/mucoid specimens to slides", a: "Schaudinn's Fixative" },
        { q: "Advantages: permanent smears can be made and stained with Trichrome, zinc preferred over copper, no mercuric chloride", a: "Modified PVA (Cu or Zn)" },
        { q: "Disadvantages: staining not consistent, organism morphology may be poor, copper-morphology of cysts and trophs is poor, zinc has better morphology but not compared to LV PVA", a: "Modified PVA (copper or zinc)" }
